  "notes": "7:1 (separate letters) carries As-Sa'di's «لم ينزلها عبثا بل لحكمة لا نعلمها», no meaning given. A book for «كتاب أنزل إليك», footsteps for «اتبعوا», night and day for «بياتا أو هم قائلون». No destruction or ruins drawn. No motif on the Prophet ﷺ. STAGING v4: c1 (1-3): a town by day; believers sit and read the Book on 2:1 and on 2:12 (As-Sa'di: a reminder by which the believers remember the straight path), the people being warned stand on the right (camera on them at 2:10 and 3:11); on 3:12 (Muyassar: you rarely take heed) they turn away. Both sides of the stage are occupied, and no camera move falls on 2:3 (to you). The Prophet is never shown; nothing on the Name. c2 (4: towns destroyed by night or at noon) stays ambient: a punishment of people, never shown, and the plan forbids drawing destruction."
